    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "反馈可能导致系统不稳定的一个常见例子是礼堂扩音系统中的音频放大器与扬声器反馈。当扬声器与传声器之间的距离减小时，若传声器放得离扬声器过近，系统就会不稳定，导致音频信号过度放大失真并产生自激啸叫。",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "A common example of the potential destabilizing effect of feedback is that of feedback in audio amplifier and speaker systems used for public address in auditoriums. As the distance between the loudspeaker and the microphone decreases, if the microphone is placed too close to the speaker, then the system will be unstable, resulting in excessive amplification and distortion of audio signals and an oscillatory squeal.",
